[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # `bad()` reads an uninitialized stack slot. When it is called directly (not
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # through `driver`), the slot's last writer is `dlopen`, so the pointer it
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # forwards depends on the loaded object's *load footprint* rather than on any
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # translated code. These controls demonstrate that by comparing two C builds
